# Optional local-inference dependencies for operators serving local/self-hosted
# subjects or A4 validators from local Apple Silicon checkpoints. This lock is a superset of
# `requirements.lock`; install it instead of the core lock on MLX machines.
# Regeneration procedure (run from repo root, with Python 3.11):
#   python -m pip install pip-tools==7.4.1
#   pip-compile --generate-hashes --allow-unsafe --output-file=requirements-local.lock requirements-local.in
# Then verify with `pip install --require-hashes -r requirements-local.lock`.
#
# `sentence-transformers==3.4.1` is intentionally absent from the active local
# lock: it requires `transformers<5`, while `mlx-lm==0.31.3` requires
# `transformers>=5`. The active codebase does not import sentence-transformers.

-r requirements.in

# --- Local-inference path (local/self-hosted subjects; A4 validators OLMo + Granite) ---
torch
transformers>=5
mlx==0.31.2
mlx-lm==0.31.3
bitsandbytes==0.49.0
ctranslate2==4.7.1
